 "description": "# Reversing Numbers\n\nTask Description: Write a program which reads a sequence and prints it in the reverse order.\nTask Constraint: n <= 100\n\n0 <= a_i < 1000\nTask Input: The input is given in the following format:\n\nn\na_1 a_2 . . . a_n\n\nn is the size of the sequence and a_i is the ith element of the sequence.\nTask Output: Print the reversed sequence in a line. Print a single space character between adjacent elements (Note that your program should not put a space character after the last element).\nTask Samples: input: 5\n1 2 3 4 5\n output: 5 4 3 2 1\ninput: 8\n3 3 4 4 5 8 7 9\n output: 9 7 8 5 4 4 3 3\n\n## Constraints\nn <= 100\n\n0 <= a_i < 1000\n\n## Input\nThe input is given in the following format:\n\nn\na_1 a_2 . . . a_n\n\nn is the size of the sequence and a_i is the ith element of the sequence.\n\n## Output\nPrint the reversed sequence in a line. Print a single space character between adjacent elements (Note that your program should not put a space character after the last element).\n\n## Examples\n['input: 5\\n1 2 3 4 5\\n output: 5 4 3 2 1', 'input: 8\\n3 3 4 4 5 8 7 9\\n output: 9 7 8 5 4 4 3 3']",
